From cc75134f62a74d0c1dd2e8cbb46f1bcbd0d5ba60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rickow <30348240+Rickow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:23:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] HSFA: plane base registers for ro9a (Hyper + Upper Arcade
 graft), sfa3hahsfa driver

- $804200-$804205: word writes handled in one step (byte mask kept for byte
  writes), nCpsGfxScroll updated only on change (FBNeo redraws planes every
  frame, so this is the equivalent of MAME's mark_all_dirty); reset to 0,
  saved in states (unchanged); HSFA_PLANS_LOG=<file> logs every change.
- Extended graphics region sized from the declared hsfa_gfx.bin
  ($2000000 + size, at least 64 MB: Upper and Hyper unchanged); hsfa_gfx.bin
  loaded and converted in place (no temporary buffer).
- New driver sfa3hahsfa (ro9a test build): Hyper files with a 48 MB
  hsfa_gfx.bin (Upper planes at $4000000), 80 MB region.
- hsfa_run: PILOTE=arcade, port of greffe_arcade/lua/tournee_arcade.lua.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
